    <!-- APPROVAL HISTORY, ADDED 2026-08-28. RelatedProcessHistoryList IS the Approval History
         list (verified live: usman-dpeg's describeLayout returns this list as name
         "ProcessSteps", label "Approval History"; twenty three+ layouts in this repo already
         carry the token, e.g. layouts/Opportunity-Opportunity Layout.layout-meta.xml and
         layouts/Disposition__c-Disposition Layout.layout-meta.xml).
         🔴 THIS BLOCK IS ONE HALF OF A TWO-FILE FIX AND IS USELESS ALONE. Underwriting__c
         renders through flexipages/Underwriting_Record_Page.flexipage-meta.xml, which gains a
         force:relatedListContainer in the same change; that component is what surfaces this
         list in Lightning. Adding the list here without the component shows nothing, and
         adding the component without this list shows nothing either -
         force:relatedListSingleContainer (used elsewhere on this same page for
         CombinedAttachments) returns INVALID_TYPE for approval history - deploys green, renders
         nothing - so relatedListContainer is the only supported route, and it renders exactly
         what this layout declares.
         WHY IT IS NEEDED AT ALL: approvalProcesses/Underwriting__c.Underwriting_Approval sets
         allowRecall=true and recordEditability=AdminOnly. Recall Approval Request exists ONLY
         on this list. Without it, a submitted Underwriting record locks with no visible pending
         approval and no recall route - see that approval process file's header for the
         mandatory pre-deploy recall of the OLD Opportunity-side pending instance, which is the
         exact trap this fixes going forward.
         The five columns are the standard Approval History set, copied from
         layouts/Opportunity-Opportunity Layout.layout-meta.xml rather than invented. -->
    <relatedLists>
        <fields>CreatedDate</fields>
        <fields>StepStatus</fields>
        <fields>OriginalActor</fields>
        <fields>Actor</fields>
        <fields>Comments</fields>
        <relatedList>RelatedProcessHistoryList</relatedList>
    </relatedLists>
